# ttyd.{{DOMAIN}} — tailnet entry point: the host shell IS the homepage.
#
# Access model — Tailscale MEMBERSHIP is the only gate, by operator choice:
#   * every path — non-tailnet sources get 403 (@not_tailnet)
#   * /        — the ttyd host shell (host systemd unit, 127.0.0.1:7681).
#                Deliberately UNAUTHENTICATED: a tailnet device that can reach
#                the vhost gets a root shell, no second credential (HTTP basic
#                auth was removed 2026-09-22 by operator request — membership
#                IS the auth). Reaching it non-tailnet is impossible: the 403
#                above runs first.
#
# The former door list (tail.html at / plus the generated /targets.json
# catalogue) was REMOVED 2026-10-29: the shell is the page, at / itself — there
# is no /ttyd subpath any more (ttyd runs without a base path).
#
# Caching: NOTHING on this vhost may be cached. `no-store` (forbids storing),
# the ETag / Last-Modified deletes (no validators left to revalidate against)
# and the legacy Pragma/Expires headers make every request hit the edge fresh.
#
# TLS — Let's Encrypt DNS-01 via Cloudflare, same as every public vhost: the
# operator asked for a trusted cert on the door too (no self-signed warning).
# The name must resolve publicly for browsers to reach it by that name; if the
# LE order cannot complete (e.g. the per-identifier rate limit), the installer
# does NOT fail — it lists scripts/ops/tailscale-https.sh as a follow-up, which
# exposes the door over Tailscale HTTPS instead (a different web address:
# https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net).
https://ttyd.{{DOMAIN}} {
    tls {
        # Fallback issuer chain: Let's Encrypt first, then Buypass Go SSL and
        # ZeroSSL — free providers tried in order, so a per-issuer rate limit
        # (5 orders/name/week on LE) never leaves a vhost without a cert.
        issuer acme https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory {
            email admin@{{DOMAIN}}
            dns cloudflare {env.CF_API_TOKEN}
        }
        issuer acme https://api.buypass.com/acme/directory {
            email admin@{{DOMAIN}}
            dns cloudflare {env.CF_API_TOKEN}
        }
        issuer acme https://acme.zerossl.com/v2/DV90 {
            email admin@{{DOMAIN}}
            dns cloudflare {env.CF_API_TOKEN}
        }
    }
    import compress
    header {
        import security_headers
        # Nothing here may be cached: a stale cached response would keep
        # serving a state the next request would not confirm.
        Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0"
        Pragma "no-cache"
        Expires "0"
        -ETag
        -Last-Modified
    }
    route {
        @not_tailnet not remote_ip 100.64.0.0/10
        respond @not_tailnet 403

        # ttyd host terminal IS the homepage — proxied as-is (ttyd runs with no
        # base path, so the request path is already the app's own).
        handle {
            reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7681 {
                transport http {
                    versions 1.1
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
